-- set-verbose-partial: `set -v` echoes each line the top-level script, stdin or `-c`
-  string supplies to stderr, but not text read by `.`/`eval`, and a `\`-continued
-  line is echoed joined.
-
-  **Repro:**
-  ```sh
-  printf 'echo a \\\n b\n' | shish -v   # echoed joined; bash echoes both lines as read
-  ```
-
 - set-histexpand-unimplemented: `struct shopt`'s `histexpand` bit
   (`src/sh.h`, `-H`) is set correctly by `set -H`/`set +H` and
   reflected back correctly in `$-`, but nothing checks it either --
